{
	vfio_cdx_set_msi_trigger(vdev, 0, 0, 0, VFIO_IRQ_SET_DATA_NONE, NULL);
}
</text>
Reason:
Adding `guard(mutex)(&vdev->cdx_irqs_lock);` at the start of vfio_cdx_set_msi_trigger() serializes all accesses to config_msi, cdx_irqs, and msi_count, making the test of config_msi atomic with the subsequent enable, disable, or trigger operations. Removing the early return in vfio_cdx_irqs_cleanup() eliminates an unsynchronized read of the lock-protected cdx_irqs pointer, relying instead on the lock‑protected check inside vfio_cdx_msi_disable(). This prevents the race condition that caused the use-after-free.

